r numerical evaluation at the substrate parameter q_0. Any generic categorical / q-deformation identities ...'. THIS block carries a four-sentence chopped variant (4 occurrences) that has LOST the enumeration entirely and split the remainder into four short declaratives; a sibling variant (9 occurrences) has additionally lost 'or complex-' and 'it draws on'. The sibling block prop:nuclear-knot-classification, in this same batch, carries the canonical form — so the divergence is visible inside one chapter. This is the sentence-splitting/de-hedging sweep signature, not authorial variation, and the content lost (which archimedean constructs trigger the wall) is exactly what makes the notice useful. Proposed: normalise all 132 to the 23-occurrence canonical wording, ideally by generating the notice rather than storing it per block. (2) MINOR, type: the display asserts F_Pauli ... 'in R', but F_Pauli is a QUOTIENT of two elements of the coefficient ring; it lies in Frac(R) (or in R only when the denominator is a unit). (3) MINOR, and the general fact is stronger than the block's: 'It is a unit when beta saturates the alternating block (fully fermionic)' is under-specified — if 'saturates' means the symmetric character vanishes, the ratio is undefined, not a unit. Related: the sibling proof block notes 'Both extremal q-dimensions equal 1' only for H_3, but this holds for EVERY n, since (n) and (1^n) are conjugate and hence have identical multisets of hook lengths, giving dim_q = [n]_q!/prod[h]_q = 1 in both cases. So the dim_q factors in the boxed formula are identically 1 and the general statement reduces to the character ratio.","history":2},{"id":"trap-performed-warmth","group":"trap","result":"pass","stale":true,"freshness":"stale","changed":["md","ts"],"at":"2026-08-21","reviewer":"agent","by":"agent:v03","history":2},{"id":"trap-rhetorical-pivot","group":"trap","result":"pass","stale":true,"freshness":"stale","changed":["md","ts"],"at":"2026-08-21","reviewer":"agent